[151.8386, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[151.884193, "o", "One Converse call, as the app would send it (illustrative; nothing is sent):\r\n\r\n  POST https://bedrock-runtime.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/model/amazon.nova-lite-v1:0/converse\r\n  Authorization: AWS4-HMAC-SHA256 Credential=... (SigV4, as in sign)\r\n  {\"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [{\"text\": \"Summarise ticket 4521 in one line.\"}]}]}\r\n\r\n"]
[151.884464, "o", "Converse is authorized as bedrock:InvokeModel. IAM runs 1 check(s) for this one call:\r\n"]
[151.885047, "o", "  1. bedrock:InvokeModel on arn:aws:bedrock:us-west-2::foundation-model/amazon.nova-lite-v1:0\r\n       ALLOWED  allowed by identity/data-science-role.json (TryAnyModelAnywhere)\r\n\r\n=> the call goes through: every check must pass. If it goes through, the bill counts input and output tokens.\r\n"]
