[167.812674, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.85823, "o", "One Converse call, as the app would send it (illustrative; nothing is sent):\r\n\r\n  POST https://bedrock-runtime.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/model/anthropic.claude-opus-4-7/converse\r\n  Authorization: Bearer <a Bedrock API key>\r\n  {\"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [{\"text\": \"Summarise ticket 4521 in one line.\"}]}]}\r\n\r\n"]
[167.858445, "o", "Converse is authorized as bedrock:InvokeModel. IAM runs 2 check(s) for this one call:\r\n"]
[167.858965, "o", "  1. bedrock:CallWithBearerToken on *  (bedrock:BearerTokenType=LONG_TERM)\r\n       ALLOWED  allowed by aws-managed/AmazonBedrockLimitedAccess-v9.json (BedrockAPIs)\r\n"]
[167.862245, "o", "  2. bedrock:InvokeModel on arn:aws:bedrock:us-east-1::foundation-model/anthropic.claude-opus-4-7\r\n       ALLOWED  allowed by aws-managed/AmazonBedrockLimitedAccess-v9.json (BedrockAPIs)\r\n\r\n=> the call goes through: every check must pass. If it goes through, the bill counts input and output tokens.\r\n"]
[167.868845, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m10\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m10\u001b[00m$ "]
